/* Analog Four MKII OS 1.56 panel keys: logical ID, name (the panel label), OS key
 * code. The firmware finds each code's panel group and bit in the unit's own
 * table at run time (remote_keys.c, locate). Names are the OS's own button
 * names, but BANK_A-H (its A-H), OCT_DOWN/OCT_UP (its OCT-/OCT+), SONG_MENU
 * (its SONG MENU; SONG is the song-mode key), the keyboard (KB_*, which it draws
 * as glyphs; codes 0x10-0x1c rising by a semitone) and the encoder pushes. */
KEY(1, "1", 0x00)
KEY(2, "2", 0x01)
KEY(3, "3", 0x02)
KEY(4, "4", 0x03)
KEY(5, "5", 0x04)
KEY(6, "6", 0x05)
